@startuml uc_overview
' Use case overview - Agentic Code Review v1.
' PlantUML is used here only because Mermaid has no native use case notation.
' Part of: ../system_analysis.md, section 1.2

title Agentic Code Review v1: Use Case Overview

left to right direction

actor "Developer\n(author)" as Dev
actor "Contributor /\nMaintainer" as Maint
actor "Regression Harness\n(corpus runner)" as Harness
actor "Project Toolchain\n(npm test, tsc)" as Tool <<system>>
actor "Model Provider\n(OpenAI-compatible,\nfree tier)" as LLM <<system>>

rectangle "Agentic Review CLI (v1 core)" {
  usecase "Review a local\nchange set" as UC1
  usecase "Resolve change scope\n(working tree, staged,\nbranch or commit)" as UC2
  usecase "Validate configuration\nand prerequisites" as UC3
  usecase "Gather related context\n(depth 0 to 1)" as UC4
  usecase "Run project checks\nand record evidence" as UC5
  usecase "Generate schema-valid\nfindings" as UC6
  usecase "Export JSON artifact" as UC7
  usecase "Measure catch rate at\npinned depth and ceiling" as UC8
  usecase "Maintain pattern rules\nand regression cases" as UC9
}

Dev --> UC1
Maint --> UC8
Maint --> UC9

UC1 ..> UC3 : <<include>>
UC1 ..> UC2 : <<include>>
UC1 ..> UC4 : <<include>>
UC1 ..> UC5 : <<include>>
UC1 ..> UC6 : <<include>>
UC7 ..> UC1 : <<extend>>
UC8 ..> UC1 : <<include>>

UC5 --> Tool
UC6 --> LLM
UC8 --> Harness

note right of Harness
  Ships inside the package (CF-8).
  Modeled as a secondary actor because
  it drives the review core as a caller,
  one corpus case at a time.
end note

note "Out of scope in v1:\n- all GitHub integration (v3)\n- context depth 2 and above (v2)\n- any write path: commit, push, auto-apply" as OOS

@enduml
